course: dictionary
lesson: 6005
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Mechanical has three main meanings: to do with machines, done without thinking, and the study of designing machines.
explain: «Robotics engineers combine mechanical engineering, electronics and coding to build machines that help with real work.» The words engineering and machines are the clues, so here mechanical means to do with machines.
explain: «Mechanical clocks spread in Europe from about 1300.» A clock is worked by moving parts like gears and wheels, so mechanical means worked by machinery. Put your meaning back into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Mechanical means to do with machines, or worked by machines with moving parts like gears, levers and wheels.
fact: Mechanical can also mean done without thinking, like a machine, out of habit.
fact: Mechanical engineering is designing and building machines.
fact: «Ada Lovelace worked with Charles Babbage on his Analytical Engine, a mechanical computer that was designed but never fully built.»
fact: «Mechanical clocks spread in Europe from about 1300, and China built a great water-driven clock tower in the 1090s.»
exercise: «Robotics engineers combine mechanical engineering, electronics and coding to build machines.» What is mechanical engineering? | Growing strawberries in a field | Writing stories for children | *Designing and building machines
exercise: «Ada Lovelace worked with Charles Babbage on his Analytical Engine, a mechanical computer.» What does mechanical mean here? | Very fast and modern | *Worked by machinery with moving parts | Done without thinking | Painted bright red
exercise: Sam says, «I gave a mechanical answer, without thinking.» What does mechanical mean here? | Carefully designed by an engineer | *Done without thinking, out of habit | Made of metal | Very loud
test: What does mechanical mean in the phrase mechanical pencil? | Made of wood | Done without thinking | *Worked by a mechanism with moving parts | Very old
test: A mechanical fault in a car is a fault with what? | The colour of the paint | The road signs | *The machinery of the car | The driver's mood
exam: Which sentence uses mechanical to mean done without thinking? | The mechanical toy had gears and wheels | *He gave a mechanical nod, not even looking up | Mechanical engineers design bridges | The mechanical clock ticked on the wall
